/**
 * Hawaiʻi community energy planning — DEMO dataset (general planning, not one project).
 *
 * GROUNDED ONLY: every signal paraphrases a perspective, anecdote, poll result,
 * survey finding or community detail from two Hawaiʻi State Energy Office reports
 * (June 2022), each cited to its page, or an approved public record (cited by URL). No invented voices; no personal names
 * (people appear only by role). Generated from claude-side source rows
 * (signals_data.py) — edit those and regenerate rather than hand-editing here.
 *
 *  - Siting Perspectives Report: https://energy.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/HSEO-Siting-Perspectives-Report_FINAL.pdf
 *  - Community Engagement Report: https://energy.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/HSEO-Community-Engagement-Report-FINAL.pdf
 *
 * Stance = attitude toward clean-energy development in the respondent's own community.
 * Sources: interviews / roundtables / workshops / workshop polls -> 'pythia'
 * (direct community voice); HSEO's own findings, online-survey statistics and
 * census/history community profiles -> 'desk' (kept IN on purpose, so the
 * dashboard can be tested on separating signal from noise); approved PUBLIC
 * RECORDS (news coverage of hearings, court + regulator decisions, published
 * letters, 2020–2022) -> 'civic', placed by location.
 * One signal = one issue, from one community, via one channel.
 *
 * Sub-dashboards: one per island (Oʻahu, Maui, Molokaʻi, Hawaiʻi Island) plus a
 * statewide one that holds EVERY signal (including Kauaʻi survey data). The
 * community is the last segment of `actor` ("… — Kahuku") for later drill-down.
 *
 * Known report quirks handled: the Lāhainā participation-poll figures repeat the
 * Kahuku figures verbatim in the report, so they are NOT used for Lāhainā; the
 * report labels Kīhei's combined ranking "Kahuku" — attributed to Kīhei here.
 */
